Maya (Presales): Quick one — Customer kickoff tomorrow. They want a short POC runbook showing: streaming SDK usage, function/tool-calls, and structured JSON outputs + answers for pricing and a SOC2/security checklist. Need a single-page howto + tiny code samples for Node and Go. Can someone stitch this together by EOD?

Jon (Eng): Yep I can draft. Hosted offering in EU region, right? Do they need ephemeral creds example and webhook handshake? Also clarify peak qps and latency SLOs.

Tess (Sales): Hosted EU yes. They said peak ~2k QPS with bursts, 99th pct latency target ~150ms. Legal flagged KMS + data retention questions — they want model inference logs not stored.

Maya (Presales): Correct on retention. Provide KMS for config and logs only. Please include a fallback plan (cheaper model variant) and batching knobs. Also include the minimum answers for the security questionnaire: data flows, incident response contact, encryption at rest/in transit.

presales-bot: Template runbook: https://redwood.internal/templates/presales/runbook-streaming.md — use the "POC checklist" section. :white_check_mark:

Jon (Eng): Draft snippet for Node streaming + function call (small):

```js
// minimal streaming + function/toolcall example
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const stream = client.chat.stream({ model: 'r-infer-2', region: 'eu' });
stream.on('data', (evt) => {
  if (evt.type === 'function_call') {
    // call external tool
    fetch('https://hooks.example.com/action', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(evt.payload) });
  }
  if (evt.type === 'message') console.log(JSON.stringify(evt.message));
});
```

Jon (Eng): And an example of structured output schema to validate on receive: {"type":"object","properties":{"intent":{"type":"string"},"entities":{"type":"array"}}} — mention we recommend the SDK's schema validation hook.

Tess (Sales): Pricing notes for runbook: give two scenarios — reserved capacity (commit) for steady base + burst bucket for peaks, and a pure hosted pay-as-you-go option. Add rough numbers: baseline for 2k QPS with batching ~ $X/day (placeholder — finance will fill).

Maya (Presales): I'll fill the commercial placeholders with the finance spreadsheet. Can you also add a short troubleshooting section: common handshake failures (CORS, auth header mismatch, stale ephemeral creds), and a sample cURL for handshake?

Jon (Eng): Putting the handshake cURL and quick auth debug steps in. cURL sample:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" \ 
  -H "Accept: text/event-stream" \ 
  https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams/chat?model=r-infer-2
```

Jon (Eng): For latency: recommend continuous batching window 10-20ms, prefix KV cache enabled, and quantized model variant for cost/latency tradeoff. Fallback policy: route to r-infer-2-small in same region when GPU pool constrained.

Tess (Sales): Legal/security checklist items to include (short):
- Data residency: EU only
- Keys: KMS-managed, HSM optional
- Logs: ephemeral by default, can be disabled
- SOC2 contact + IR process summary

Maya (Presales): Perfect. I'll consolidate and post a one-page runbook in the drive + paste summary here. Will ping finance/legal for numbers and SOC2 blurb. Thanks — team, tag me with @Maya when ready. :rocket:

